   "title": "READ ME",
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "PromptForge H3 - everything in one workflow (left to right)\n\n1. LOADER: model (10Eros Max beta7 etc.), text encoder, VAEs. The 2x detail VAE decodes every part. 'Prompt writer' is the language model that writes each part's prompt.\n2. STORY: the general prompt + one box per part (press + / -). Everything you write goes here; the prompt writer turns it into H3 prompts.\n3. REFERENCES / FIRST FRAME / VOICE / EXTEND A VIDEO: the optional inputs.\n4. SETTINGS: size and length, how parts join, sampling, second stage, preview, speed.\n5. GENERATE makes the parts and returns the frames and sound. 6. SAVE VIDEO saves them.\n\nMODES - pick one by bypassing nodes (select a node, Ctrl+B). Bypassed nodes are the optional ones:\n- Text to video: bypass all the Load nodes and the Extend nodes; write the Story.\n- Image to video: un-bypass 'First frame' and pick the picture.\n- Characters / reference to video: un-bypass the character pictures (their descriptions go to the prompt writer too). Refer to them as <Picture 1>, <Picture 2> in the story.\n- Voice: un-bypass the voice sample.\n- Extend a video: un-bypass the three 'Video to extend' nodes; the new parts continue it and the result contains both.\n- Quick preview: bypass 'Second Stage' (first pass only, much faster); un-bypass it for the full two-pass result.\n- Endless: raise the number of parts in the Story (each part is 5 or 10 seconds).\n- Smoother motion: un-bypass the interpolation node and set Save Video frame_rate to 48.\n\nDefaults follow the 10Eros Max beta7 recommendations: er_sde + sgm_uniform, 8 steps, cfg 1, shift 12/3, 90% sparse attention (VSA), second pass 3 steps from sigma 0.9035. For other H3 models turn 'sparse_attention' off in Speed and Memory."
   ],
   "widgets_values_named": {
    "text": "PromptForge H3 - everything in one workflow (left to right)\n\n1. LOADER: model (10Eros Max beta7 etc.), text encoder, VAEs. The 2x detail VAE decodes every part. 'Prompt writer' is the language model that writes each part's prompt.\n2. STORY: the general prompt + one box per part (press + / -). Everything you write goes here; the prompt writer turns it into H3 prompts.\n3. REFERENCES / FIRST FRAME / VOICE / EXTEND A VIDEO: the optional inputs.\n4. SETTINGS: size and length, how parts join, sampling, second stage, preview, speed.\n5. GENERATE makes the parts and returns the frames and sound. 6. SAVE VIDEO saves them.\n\nMODES - pick one by bypassing nodes (select a node, Ctrl+B). Bypassed nodes are the optional ones:\n- Text to video: bypass all the Load nodes and the Extend nodes; write the Story.\n- Image to video: un-bypass 'First frame' and pick the picture.\n- Characters / reference to video: un-bypass the character pictures (their descriptions go to the prompt writer too). Refer to them as <Picture 1>, <Picture 2> in the story.\n- Voice: un-bypass the voice sample.\n- Extend a video: un-bypass the three 'Video to extend' nodes; the new parts continue it and the result contains both.\n- Quick preview: bypass 'Second Stage' (first pass only, much faster); un-bypass it for the full two-pass result.\n- Endless: raise the number of parts in the Story (each part is 5 or 10 seconds).\n- Smoother motion: un-bypass the interpolation node and set Save Video frame_rate to 48.\n\nDefaults follow the 10Eros Max beta7 recommendations: er_sde + sgm_uniform, 8 steps, cfg 1, shift 12/3, 90% sparse attention (VSA), second pass 3 steps from sigma 0.9035. For other H3 models turn 'sparse_attention' off in Speed and Memory."
   },
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  }
